! I-Box 1 diagnostic program, octal 5123.00 through 5461.40 -- TWENTY
! consecutive test groups from docs/ja_ax1a_ibox-1.pdf pp.43-51, the
! deck's entire index-branching section plus the SIC and indicator
! groups that follow it, transcribed VERBATIM as one contiguous span at
! the listing's own addresses, with the deck's own pass/fail mechanism
! intact throughout:
!
!   CB          IBR..IBR9       5123.00  (p.43 bottom / p.44)
!   CB+         IBR10..IBR19    5136.00
!   CBH         IBR20..IBR29    5151.00
!   CB-         IBR30..IBR39    5164.00
!   CBZ         IBR40..IBR53    5177.00
!   CBZ+        IBR54..IBR67    5211.00  (uses CNOP)
!   CBZ-        IBR68..IBR81    5223.00
!   CBZH        IBR82..IBR95    5235.00  (uses CNOP)
!   CBR         IBR96..IBR101   5247.00
!   CBR+        IBR102..IBR108  5261.00  "count, branch refill, + add one to value"
!   CBR-        IBR109..IBR115  5276.00  "... sub one from value"
!   CBRH        IBR116..IBR122  5312.00  "... add half to value"
!   CBRZ        IBR123..IBR140  5326.00  "count, branch on zero, + refill"
!   CBRZ+       IBR141..IBR158  5343.00
!   CBRZ-       IBR159..IBR176  5360.00
!   CBRZH       IBR177..IBR194  5375.00
!   SIC-CB      ISCB..ISCBH     5412.00
!   SIC-CBZ     ISCB5..ISCBK    5421.00
!   SIC-B,ZIND  ISBI..ISBXW     5432.40
!   SIC-B,IND   ISBI5..ISBIK    5443.00
!   (indicators) WEN2/WEN/VEN   5454.00  (WEN6/WEN7 at 6102/6103)
!
! Above 5123.00 the deck tests LR/SR against the indicator register
! ("LOAD + STORE REFILL IN INTERNAL MEMORY", SR,$X1,$IND+.32), a store
! this model does not honor (bsv/README.md, word 11) -- the span starts
! at the first group below that. Grown in three steps: pp.50-51, then
! pp.46-49 (see git history for the two earlier files this supersedes),
! then pp.43-46 once the assembler had CNOP.
!
! Control flow, as the deck wrote it. In the count-and-branch groups
! every "B,$" or "BD,$" is a hang, and the group proves itself by
! storing X1's whole index word over one of them with SX ("SX TO TEST
! VALUE" / "SX FOR VALUE TEST"): the XW literal it started from puts a
! bit-address like IBR106+(8).04 in the value field, chosen so that the
! value the variant SHOULD have produced (two CBR+ = +2.0 words, five
! CBRZH = +2.40, two CBR- = -2.0 ...) reads as "BD,<the next hang>"
! when executed as an instruction -- so a correct value branches on,
! a wrong one lands on a hang. The count-to-zero call then refills X1
! from a second XW whose value reads as "BD,<the group's NOP-valued VF
! pair>", stored the same way ("SX + TEST FOR REFILL"), and the chain
! walks: value-test hang -> refill-test hang -> VF NOPs -> next group.
! The SIC groups are described in ibox1_sic_cb_cbz.strap's header; the
! SIC-B groups' own detail is in verify_ibox1_listing.py's ROWS_SICB
! comment. The whole span ends where
! VEN's own "BRGZZ,$+1.0" lands, 5462.00, the start of the (floating-
! point, out of scope) "Y-Z CONTROL SEQUENCES" test -- the ONE
! substituted instruction here is a BEW,$ at that address.
!
! What the count-and-branch groups pin down that no earlier test
! could: the H / + / - value increments of the CB family. Reference
! Manual p.41's table says H adds "one in bit position 18" of the
! value field and +/- add or subtract "one in bit position 17" -- i.e.
! a half-word (32 bits) and a word (64 bits) of bit address -- and the
! listing's own arithmetic agrees (IBRA23's value 5405.44 plus five
! halves is 5410.04, exactly IBR193+.04, where its comment says the
! value test must land). bsv/README.md had recorded the model's
! mapping (+1/+2/-2 raw bit units) as an unconfirmed best-effort
! reading; it was wrong by a factor of 32, and this span is the test
! that would have hung at IBR106 under it.
!
! Expected final state (ibox1_expected.py): halt PC 5462.00; every
! SX-stored word (value-test words as X1's full index word at that
! point, refill-test words as copies of the refill XW); every SIC- or
! SV-rewritten hang of the p.50-51 groups.
!
! Listing text restored from the printout's %..= to (..). Two scan
! readings are noted in verify_ibox1_listing.py (BZXVLZ,ISBI5 and
! IBR184's CBRZH). The "66"/"6"/"666" marks in the listing's right
! margin are ignored.
!
! Bug injections, observed results:
!   C. LX without index-indicator setting (StretchExecute.bsv DirIndex
!      arm): 6 of 13 fail on the pp.50-51 half alone -- PC parks at
!      ISBIC, the hang after BZXCZ (the preceding SV had left XCZ on).
!   D. CB half/one units back to 1/2/-2 raw bits: 26 of 28 fail -- PC
!      parks at IBR106 (the first incrementing variant's value test),
!      only CBR's two v=00 words (IBR100, IBR107) still pass. Exactly
!      as predicted.
! Both reverted by targeted un-patch; full suite green. The pp.43-46
! groups added afterwards (CB..CBZH, no refill) passed 8/8 on their
! first run with no model change needed beyond CNOP in the assembler.

        SLC, (8)5123.0
